ndidates who were up there on the  podium what struck you well first of all  I was I was struck by what I have always  sense which is that we have a remarkably  rich and talented field of candidates it  doesn't bother me one bit that there are  a lot of them you wish you were there  the possibility you could beat all of  them that's not how I was thinking about  it although when I was thinking about it  many months ago one of the questions was  how do you break through in a field this  large and this talented without being a  celebrity or or sensationalist and I'm  none of those things nights what did you  what sir I thought that the  first night one contrast has jumped out  was that they didn't speak about the  incumbent president should they and at  the second night they did a live long  and frankly you know and I think I may  be in a minority in this respect I don't  think Democrats should spend their time  on on President Trump it's not it I  don't say that as a matter of disrespect  yeah the the the impact and the and  frankly in my view the hurt and harm  that the president has done in the  nation is a matter of record that is not  what is going to win the election for  Democrats but will win the election for  Democrats is a positive alternative  agenda that speaks to how things will be  different not just how we will remove  the incumbent and go back to the way we  used to do things would be another  reason for you to get in the race  Governor Patrick no regrets on the  record well Patrick thank you so much

